issues/018 -- {list, float} merged into one variable makes FA specialize a container method against a scalar. NOT the BOXING shape (that one is now refused cleanly): this emits NO boxing violation and dies on an internal assertion from inside the builtin library, "sizeof_element of non-container type". What it needs is a user-facing diagnostic naming the variable and its union (shedskin rejects it too; NOT plcfrs shape -- see ifa/issues/105)
